alias for numeric priority in batch commands\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"CLI DX: accept P1/P2/P3 format as alias for numeric priority in batch commands\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #666 (d561c38b07f9f67f56ca3395e1c8e79e4717e904): batch argv normalization now accepts P1/P2/P3 (P1-P5 case-insensitive) for numeric priority parameters while preserving literal P-notation for non-numeric priority options. Added unit + integration coverage in tests/batch-exec-engine.test.ts. Full regression verified (npm test: 173 files, 3632 passed, 0 failed) and PR CI checks passed on current HEAD before merge. AC coverage path: N/A (task has no spec_ref).\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"session_id\": \"01KJVT52QN7EH1GVPZ9QP1SD53\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-03-03T06:43:29.940Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-03-04T07:06:09.618Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-03-04T08:49:57.796Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-03-04T08:58:42.278Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJVTVNW9D7CEF66BV6APX2V1\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-04T07:09:09.385Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Execution context:\\n- Background: Batch payloads currently fail when priority is provided as P-notation for commands that expect numeric 1-5.\\n- Scope: Add batch-layer normalization so priority values P1/P2/P3 (and existing P1-P5 format) are accepted where numeric priority options are expected.\\n- Files: src/cli/batch-exec.ts and tests/batch-exec-engine.test.ts.\\n- Verification: run targeted Vitest for batch exec engine, then run kspec validate and full tests as needed for confidence.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJVVD621RDA18JVDRYXF8B2W\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-04T07:18:43.010Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"WIP checkpoint committed on branch feat/task-batch-priority-p-alias at commit 6946452be. Files: src/cli/batch-exec.ts, tests/batch-exec-engine.test.ts.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJW0KWKCTT4R91RZZYDZBE4G\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-04T08:49:45.580Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented batch-layer priority alias normalization for numeric priority params in src/cli/batch-exec.ts (accepts P1-P5 / p1-p5 -> 1-5 only when command metadata indicates numeric priority). Added unit/integration coverage in tests/batch-exec-engine.test.ts, including guard that non-numeric priority options keep literal values. Validation: npm run test -- tests/batch-exec-engine.test.ts (pass), npm test (pass: 173 files, 3632 tests). Context: moved work from stale branch base to clean branch feat/task-batch-priority-p-alias-clean to avoid PR conflation.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJW0NKN3Q9GW9MQS2YBBCBN2\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-04T08:50:41.955Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Submitted for review in PR #666 (https://github.com/kynetic-ai/kynetic-spec/pull/666) from branch feat/task-batch-priority-p-alias-clean. Commits: 14af23c14 (batch alias normalization) and 1af52786b (test robustness update).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJS7016KEJ4Q7B4CTX5P9W18\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"CLI DX: accept spec_ref as alias for spec-ref in batch commands\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"CLI DX: accept spec_ref as alias for spec-ref in batch commands\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"No implementation delta required. Verified on 2026-03-03 that batch args accept spec_ref alias for --spec-ref in task add/task set (dry-run succeeds) and existing focused test coverage passes.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"session_id\": \"01KJVXPW876HS5DEF0SF5N218F\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-03-03T06:43:31.667Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-03-04T08:00:19.688Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-03-04T08:00:56.210Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-03-04T08:01:00.569Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJVXSBJD5V09MAAVJJPTYA7S\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-04T08:00:19.021Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Execution context:\\\\n- Background: task asks for spec_ref alias compatibility in batch command args.\\\\n- Scope: verify alias behavior and add/fix code only if failing.\\\\n- Files: src/cli/batch-exec.ts and tests/batch-exec-engine.test.ts if changes are needed.\\\\n- Verification: batch dry-run command(s) + focused vitest coverage.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJVXT5G087NTVWZRJ1NTZQ0V\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-04T08:00:45.568Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Verified behavior already implemented on main:\\\\n- kspec batch --dry-run with args.spec_ref for task add succeeds.\\\\n- kspec batch --dry-run with args.spec_ref for task set succeeds.\\\\n- Focused regression test passes: vitest batch-exec-engine 'handles underscore args for kebab-case options'.\\\\nNo code changes required for this task.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJS702WDPKNN01FQ3CEYB822\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"CLI DX: accept tags as alias for tag in batch commands\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"CLI DX: accept tags as alias for tag in batch commands\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #667. Added batch argument alias support for tags->tag with tests covering argv translation and persisted tags.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"session_id\": \"01KJW0P89KS67VP1G9QWW6QCWJ\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-03-03T06:43:33.388Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-03-04T08:59:50.030Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-03-04T09:07:46.868Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-03-04T09:39:54.655Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJW16F2CNHXAFZ4XFHWPZ8G3\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-04T08:59:54.316Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Execution context:\\n- Background: batch currently validates option keys strictly, so plural 'tags' is rejected even when CLI option is '--tag'.\\n- Scope: accept 'tags' as alias for 'tag' in batch command args without changing non-batch command behavior.\\n- Files: src/cli/batch-exec.ts and batch execution tests.\\n- Verification: targeted batch tests plus full test suite checks.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJW1M8T3QMPGAVWFX0YZ9E5X\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-04T09:07:26.659Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented batch arg alias resolution for tags->tag in validation and argv translation. Added unit and integration coverage in batch-exec-engine tests; verified alias emits --tag and persists inbox tags.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJW1MD1KMA0JRNQ57DPM2DVH\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-04T09:07:30.996Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Validation check: kspec validate currently fails from pre-existing project metadata/reference issues (duplicate @observations slug and missing skills.observations content), unrelated to this task's batch alias changes.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJS7NZ5AVXWVS04A7CDF9JG9\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Stream agent text output to stdout in kspec agent run\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"kspec agent run currently calls runInvocation() without an onUpdate callback, so the agent's text response is never printed to the terminal. The user sees nothing until completion, when only the session ID and outcome are shown.\\n\\nFix: In src/cli/commands/agent.ts (around line 363), pass an onUpdate handler to runInvocation that prints text content blocks to stdout as they arrive. In --json mode, suppress streaming. At the end, still output the session summary.\\n\\nImplementation details:\\n- runInvocation accepts onUpdate?: (update: SessionUpdate) => void\\n- SessionUpdate events with content arrays contain text blocks (type: 'text')\\n- In interactive mode: process.stdout.write(block.text) for each text block\\n- In --json mode: skip the onUpdate handler entirely\\n- SessionUpdate type is imported from src/acp/index.ts\\n\\nRelevant files:\\n- src/cli/commands/agent.ts — add onUpdate to runInvocation call (line ~363)\\n- src/agent-runtime/invocation.ts — runInvocation signature with onUpdate\\n- src/acp/index.ts — SessionUpdate type definition\\n\\nTest: E2E or integration test that runs kspec agent run and verifies stdout contains agent text output.\\n\\nSpec ACs to cover: @cli-agent-commands ac-12 (interactive streaming), ac-11 (JSON suppression)\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@cli-agent-commands\",\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #644. Streaming implementation: onUpdate passed to runInvocation in interactive mode, suppressed in --json mode via isJsonMode() conditional. ac-11 and ac-12 covered with non-trivially-true tests — ac-11 uses setJsonMode(true)+isJsonMode() to replicate agent.ts decision logic and asserts onUpdate is undefined; ac-12 proves mock sends chunks when onUpdate is real.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"cli\",\n      \"agent\",\n      \"dx\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"session_id\": \"01KJS9H76EZZB742ZEV9GGR8XB\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-03-03T06:55:30.474Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-03-03T18:13:57.919Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-03-03T18:13:59.185Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-03-03T18:31:03.753Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJTCXHYW2G9EZ34699P5GHZF\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-03T17:46:16.413Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented ac-11 and ac-12: added onUpdate handler to runInvocation call in src/cli/commands/agent.ts. In interactive mode, streams agent_message_chunk text content to stdout as it arrives. In --json mode, onUpdate is undefined so nothing streams. Added a newline after streaming to separate output from the completion summary. Tests added to cli-agent-commands.test.ts using existing mock ACP adapter with MOCK_ACP_RESPONSE_TEXT env var.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJTDAQ7VYQDV957RQAX5422J\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-03T17:53:27.803Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Spec work: Added ac-13..ac-16 to @cli-agent-commands for kspec agent dispatch watch command. Added ac-8 to @daemon-agent-dispatch for WebSocket text chunk broadcasting. The dispatch watch feature requires two implementation pieces: (1) daemon broadcasts agent_text_chunk events via existing WebSocket PubSub when dispatch engine text arrives, (2) new kspec agent dispatch watch subcommand that connects to daemon WS and tails output. Will be a separate task.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJTE14Z9CNQCMHQFPVK0S7AY\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-03T18:05:42.761Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Review findings: AC-11 test does not exercise the CLI-level isJsonMode() branch. The collected array is declared but never populated — onUpdate: undefined means nothing fills it, so expect(collected).toHaveLength(0) is trivially true. The test should call kspec('agent run <agent> prompt --json', testDir) via the CLI runner and assert stdout is valid JSON with no streaming text, similar to the dry-run --json test at line 609. The isJsonMode() conditional in agent.ts is currently untested at the CLI level.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJTEG2P14VC6GRKZ3ZP1E137\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-03T18:13:51.937Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Fix cycle 1: replaced false-positive ac-11 test. Old test passed onUpdate:undefined manually and asserted empty collected array (trivially true). New test uses setJsonMode(true)+isJsonMode() to replicate agent.ts decision logic, then asserts expect(onUpdate).toBeUndefined(). Combined with ac-12 (proves mock sends chunks when onUpdate is real), the pair is non-trivially true.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJS7PDW5GQQX9WQ2C7C1JNRX\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Add --text flag to kspec session log show to replay agent output\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"kspec session log show has no way to read the actual text response from a completed agent invocation. The session.update events contain content blocks with the agent's text, but --events only shows event metadata, not content.\\n\\nFix: Add a --text flag to session log show that extracts and prints the assistant text from session.update events in chronological order.\\n\\nImplementation details:\\n- Events are stored in .kspec/sessions/<session-id>/events.jsonl\\n- Filter for type === 'session.update'\\n- From each event's data.content array, collect blocks with type === 'text'\\n- Print the text in order to stdout (no extra formatting — just the content)\\n- --text and --events are independent flags (both can be used together or separately)\\n- Externalized blobs: if content is a blob pointer, resolve it (same logic as --resolve-blobs)\\n\\nRelevant files:\\n- src/cli/commands/session/log.ts — session log show command\\n- src/session/ — session event reading utilities\\n\\nWorkaround (until fixed):\\n  cat .kspec/sessions/<id>/events.jsonl | python3 -c \\\"\\n  import sys, json\\n  for line in sys.stdin:\\n    e = json.loads(line)\\n    if e.get('type') == 'session.update':\\n      for block in (e.get('data',{}).get('content') or []):\\n        if isinstance(block, dict) and block.get('type') == 'text':\\n          print(block.get('text',''), end='')\\n  \\\"\\n\\nTest: Integration test that creates a session with known text output and verifies --text prints it.\\n\\nSpec ACs to cover: @session-log-show ac-11 (--text flag replays assistant text)\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@session-log-show\",\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #668 (commit 74b5e76e5452cf295f1a20bd3d114d540d22f6b8): added --text replay mode to session log show with blob resolution support and AC-covered tests.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"cli\",\n      \"session\",\n      \"dx\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"session_id\": \"01KJW3GKF2X1NY0RC6N3AXQM49\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-03-03T06:55:45.541Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-03-04T09:41:58.390Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-03-04T09:50:20.963Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-03-04T10:26:59.765Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJW3KEPZ323FHC2SJ5QCZQMP\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-04T09:41:57.088Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Execution context:\\n- Background: replaying assistant response text from session logs currently requires manual parsing of events.jsonl.\\n- Scope: add --text to session log show, extract text from session.update content structures, support blob resolution parity, and add integration tests.\\n- Files: src/cli/commands/session/commands.ts, src/cli/commands/session/log.ts, tests/session-log-show.test.ts.\\n- Verification: targeted session-log-show tests plus kspec validate and relevant test shard.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJW425QR95RQZ54W0GX1Z36A\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-04T09:49:59.416Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented --text replay for session log show:\\n- Added --text flag to session log show command.\\n- Extracts text from session.update data.content blocks in event order.\\n- Resolves externalized blob pointers before extracting text, so replay includes full content.\\n- Kept --events and --text independent; JSON output can include both events and text.\\n- In text mode, --text alone outputs raw replay content with no extra formatting.\\n\\nTests:\\n- Added AC coverage in tests/session-log-show.test.ts for @session-log-show ac-11 and --json --text --events coexistence.\\n- Verified with npx vitest run tests/session-log-show.test.ts.\\n- Verified full suite via npm run test:shard1, npm run test:shard2, npm run test:shard3.\\n- npm run typecheck passes.\\n\\nValidation note:\\n- kspec validate currently fails due pre-existing repo-wide meta/reference issues unrelated to this task (missing observations skill file, duplicate @observations slug, existing alignment/completeness warnings).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJW4BDJJWPZ69K9JK3YH7W0T\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-04T09:55:02.354Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Submitted for review in PR #668: https://github.com/kynetic-ai/kynetic-spec/pull/668\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJS8B9QSQS53CT4DR2YHP1A8\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Add dispatch rule flags to kspec meta add agent / meta set\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"kspec meta add agent and kspec meta set have no way to set dispatch rules — the most critical field for wiring agents to task lifecycle events. Direct YAML editing is required, violating the CLI-only convention. Add --add-dispatch-rule <json>, --remove-dispatch-rule <on>, --clear-dispatch-rules to both commands. Schema in src/schema/meta.ts (AgentDispatchRuleSchema). Relevant files: src/cli/commands/meta.ts. Spec AC: @agent-definition-schema ac-12\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@agent-definition-schema\",\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #669: added --add-dispatch-rule, --remove-dispatch-rule, and --clear-dispatch-rules to kspec meta add agent and kspec meta set with schema validation (AgentDispatchRuleSchema/AgentDispatchEventSchema) plus integration coverage for append/remove/clear and invalid inputs. AC coverage for @agent-definition-schema ac-1..ac-12 and inherited trait ACs verified (with explicit N/A annotations where applicable).\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"cli\",\n      \"agent\",\n      \"dx\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"session_id\": \"01KJW67S4NJE0CPDCB3YWPD4KX\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-03-03T07:07:09.433Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-03-04T10:28:38.127Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-03-04T10:45:31.457Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-03-04T10:52:33.417Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJS8K98W47H65FHCDBV2KESR\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-03T07:11:31.100Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Manually added dispatch rules to worker and reviewer agents in kynetic.meta.yaml since CLI does not yet support --add-dispatch-rule. Worker: task.ready + task.needs_work with automation:eligible filter. Reviewer: task.pending_review. This task still needed to add CLI flag support.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJS8RV6V9KG4Y1E63ZFFHQPZ\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-03T07:14:33.307Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Fixed worker skill slug: kspec-task-work -> task-work. Runtime resolves from .kspec/skills/<id>/SKILL.md so bare slug is required, not the kspec- prefixed rendered name. Also need --remove-skill on meta set (no way to remove skills via CLI currently).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJW6931NHWTJZ45NXSV7NKCH\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-04T10:28:43.189Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Execution context:\\n- Background: CLI currently requires manual YAML edits to manage agent dispatch rules.\\n- Scope: add dispatch rule mutation flags to both meta add agent and meta set, with validation + tests.\\n- Files: src/cli/commands/meta.ts and related tests under tests/.\\n- Verification: targeted meta command tests + full validate/test command before submit.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJW6ZWD0S7794F456BX9S582\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-04T10:41:10.048Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented AC-12 dispatch rule CLI mutations:\\n- Added --add-dispatch-rule (repeatable JSON), --remove-dispatch-rule <event>, and --clear-dispatch-rules to both meta add agent and meta set.\\n- Parsed/validated add payloads with AgentDispatchRuleSchema and remove event with AgentDispatchEventSchema.\\n- Added integration tests for append/remove/clear and invalid JSON/event errors in tests/meta.test.ts.\\nVerification:\\n- npx vitest run tests/meta.test.ts (pass)\\n- npm test (pass: 173 files, 3641 tests)\\n- kspec validate still reports pre-existing repo-wide schema/reference/alignment issues unrelated to this task.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJW780BZ9BZYCY07YTJ4537D\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-04T10:45:36.256Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Submitted for review in PR #669: https://github.com/kynetic-ai/kynetic-spec/pull/669\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJS8BAWP2WNCD003DQX75GKY\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Deprecate kspec ralph — show migration message pointing to kspec agent\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"kspec ralph still exists in src/cli/commands/ralph.ts. Per @ralph-replacement ac-1, replace the command body with a deprecation message listing equivalent kspec agent commands: kspec ralph run -> kspec agent dispatch start, kspec ralph end-loop -> kspec agent end-loop. Exit with code 1. Relevant file: src/cli/commands/ralph.ts. Spec AC: @ralph-replacement ac-1\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@ralph-replacement\",\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\