ult: this task’s scope is already implemented on main via prior migration work (PR #640). Confirmed deleted legacy tests: tests/ralph.test.ts, tests/ralph-loop-errors.test.ts, tests/ralph-wrap-up.test.ts, tests/ralph-context-refresh.test.ts. Confirmed equivalent replacement coverage by running: npm run test -- tests/agent-dispatch-engine.test.ts tests/agent-invocation-lifecycle.test.ts tests/cli-agent-commands.test.ts tests/ralph-replacement.test.ts (121 tests passed). kspec validate currently reports pre-existing repository-wide schema/reference issues unrelated to this task (duplicate @observations slug and missing .kspec/skills/observations/SKILL.md).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJWCTTXX04ATJGCQDYAZ8GQB\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-04T12:23:16.157Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Autonomous pending_review dispatch processed on 2026-03-04. Task was already completed (completed_at 2026-03-04T12:17:11.246Z) with closure linked to merged PR #640. Verified no active PR for this task scope, confirmed PR #640 is MERGED, and reran full regression suite (npm test: 173 files passed, 3641 tests passed, 3 skipped). No additional transition required.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJS8BFDFFNC3PVTNHRRPZSVZ\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Update workflows to remove ralph references and use agent dispatch concepts\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Workflow definitions task-work-loop, pr-review-loop, session-reflect-loop still reference ralph concepts. Per @ralph-replacement ac-4, update to reference kspec agent dispatch commands. Also regenerate kspec-agents.md after. Spec AC: @ralph-replacement ac-4\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@ralph-replacement\",\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"docs\",\n      \"workflow\",\n      \"ralph\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-03-03T07:07:15.247Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJX36BZ6G4KZGDZ3B2FDD30T\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-04T18:54:02.726Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Carry-forward requirement from PR #664: when replacing ralph loop wording with agent dispatch concepts, preserve explicit per-task branch isolation guidance (create/switch dedicated task branch before file edits) so worker/reviewer/fix-cycle flows avoid cross-task branch contamination.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"manual_only\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJS8BGJA457W8X7F28MWFYBP\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Update skills to reference agent runtime instead of ralph\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Skills kspec:task-work, codex, eval-agents, pr-review still reference kspec ralph commands. Per @ralph-replacement ac-5, update to reference kspec agent commands and agent dispatch concepts. Core skills in templates/skills/, project skills in .kspec/skills/. Run kspec skill render after. Spec AC: @ralph-replacement ac-5\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@ralph-replacement\",\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"docs\",\n      \"skills\",\n      \"ralph\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-03-03T07:07:16.426Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJX36D7GEYZVQVGV5RJV02T2\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-04T18:54:04.017Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Carry-forward requirement from PR #664: keep branch-isolation step in task-work/pr-review/codex/eval-agents skill updates. Runtime guidance must state: after task start and before edits, create/switch to dedicated task branch.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"manual_only\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJS8V7THVJ8GRF1M6XVZH9FY\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Evaluate and improve dispatch prompt for worker and reviewer agents\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"When the dispatch engine fires an agent, the base prompt is either agent.prompt_template or 'Work on task @ref' (dispatch.ts:662). The skill content is then appended by buildPromptWithSkills.\\n\\nEvaluate whether this is sufficient context for the agent to orient itself, or whether the dispatch prompt should include richer context such as:\\n- Task title and description\\n- Spec ref and AC summary\\n- Trigger event (task.ready vs task.needs_work) so agent knows if it is starting fresh or handling a fix cycle\\n- For reviewer: the PR URL if already known\\n\\nSuggested approach:\\n1. Run a real dispatch invocation (kspec agent run worker --task @some-eligible-task) and observe behavior in session log\\n2. If agent struggles to orient: enrich the prompt template in dispatch.ts or add prompt_template to worker/reviewer agent definitions in kynetic.meta.yaml\\n3. Consider whether prompt_template should support interpolation variables (e.g. {{task_ref}}, {{task_title}}, {{trigger}})\\n\\nRelevant files:\\n- src/agent-runtime/dispatch.ts line 662 — prompt construction\\n- src/agent-runtime/prompts.ts — buildPromptWithSkills\\n- .kspec/kynetic.meta.yaml — worker/reviewer agent definitions (prompt_template field)\\n\\nThis is intentionally a manual evaluation task — run a real invocation first, then decide what to fix.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": \"@01KJXDGN\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #679. Added dispatch prompt orientation context (task title/trigger, fix-cycle notes, reviewer review_url), prompt_template {{variable}} interpolation, task review_url schema/CLI support (submit/set/get), and fixed empty --review-url validation edge case. AC coverage verified for @agent-dispatch-engine ac-13..ac-16 and @task-submit ac-submit-1..ac-submit-3.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"agent\",\n      \"dx\",\n      \"dispatch\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"review_url\": \"https://github.com/kynetic-ai/kynetic-spec/pull/679\",\n    \"session_id\": \"01KJVJ866FAH439DBR6PRGBWGJ\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-03-03T07:15:51.761Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-03-04T22:30:16.969Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-03-04T22:30:18.530Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-03-04T22:38:32.584Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJXE0B8B8JHZSDBN2VD2S99Z\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-04T22:02:59.728Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implementation complete. Changes: (1) review_url field on TaskSchema + TaskInputSchema, (2) --review-url flag on task submit + task set with URL validation, (3) review_url display in formatTaskDetails, (4) Exported interpolateTemplate + buildOrientationContext helpers in dispatch.ts, (5) Fixed change.task data flow for API-event path, (6) Orientation context in dispatch prompts: task title, trigger meaning, fix-cycle notes (last 3, 200 char cap), review URL for reviewer. All 52 new+existing tests pass.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJXF657NXBJ6WY8MT8F675S3\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-04T22:23:38.741Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Review findings: MUST-FIX: task submit accepts empty --review-url and still transitions state, violating @task-submit ac-submit-3.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJXFJ1M137HGMEZWW8EM3RPS\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-04T22:30:08.258Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Fixed empty --review-url bypass: changed truthy check to !== undefined in task submit (line 1631), matching existing pattern in task set. Also fixed spread at line 1661. Added test for empty-string rejection. All 9 review_url tests + 44 dispatch tests pass.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"manual_only\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJS90FR4GQVQQYA4QM2XJZ1W\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Rewrite {skill:foo} references to adapter-specific format when injecting skills into agent prompt\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"When buildPromptWithSkills injects skill content into the agent prompt, cross-skill references like {skill:writing-specs} or {skill:plan} are passed through as-is. These are meaningless to the agent unless it knows the format.\\n\\nAdapters have different invocation formats:\\n- claude-agent-acp  -> /skill-name  (Claude Code slash commands, e.g. /kspec:task-work)\\n- codex-acp         -> $skill-name  (Codex CLI format)\\n- unknown/fallback  -> leave {skill:foo} as-is\\n\\nFix: In src/agent-runtime/prompts.ts, after resolving skill content, apply a substitution pass over the concatenated prompt replacing {skill:foo} with the adapter-appropriate format. The adapter ID is available via agent.adapter (resolved via resolveAdapter in src/agents/adapters.ts).\\n\\nNote: Claude Code uses kspec: namespace prefix for kspec skills (e.g. /kspec:task-work not /task-work). Check .agents/skills/ directory naming convention and the skill manifest to understand the correct prefix.\\n\\nRelevant files:\\n- src/agent-runtime/prompts.ts  — resolveSkills, buildPromptWithSkills\\n- src/agents/adapters.ts        — adapter resolution, adapter IDs\\n- src/schema/meta.ts            — AgentSchema.adapter field, platform_config\\n- .agents/skills/               — rendered skill names (kspec-task-work -> /kspec:task-work)\\n\\nSpec AC: @agent-invocation-lifecycle ac-10\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@agent-invocation-lifecycle\",\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": null,\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"agent\",\n      \"skills\",\n      \"dx\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-03-03T07:18:43.716Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-03-04T00:44:07.706Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-03-04T00:49:18.835Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-03-04T00:58:20.181Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJV4TMERCY7KDMJE36P4QY1E\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-04T00:44:06.488Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Execution context:\\n- Background: Skill references in injected prompts currently remain in portable {skill:foo} form and are not adapter-friendly for invocation agents.\\n- Scope: Add adapter-aware skill reference rewriting during prompt build and cover behavior with AC-annotated tests.\\n- Files: src/agent-runtime/prompts.ts, src/agent-runtime/invocation.ts, src/cli/commands/agent.ts, tests/agent-invocation-lifecycle.test.ts.\\n- Verification: npm test -- tests/agent-invocation-lifecycle.test.ts and targeted CLI dry-run checks via tests for prompt building.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJV53DW3TSK6HJ5SRC8PC78Z\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-04T00:48:54.659Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented adapter-aware skill token rewriting in buildPromptWithSkills.\\n- Added adapterId-aware substitution of {skill:foo} for claude-agent-acp/claude-code-acp and codex-acp.\\n- Mapping checks .agents/skills naming (kspec-* directories) so core skills become /kspec:<id> (Claude) and -<id> (Codex); non-core references become /<id> or $<id>.\\n- Unknown adapters keep portable {skill:foo} tokens unchanged.\\n- Passed adapterId from runtime invocation and CLI agent dry-run path.\\n- Added AC-10 tests in tests/agent-invocation-lifecycle.test.ts for Claude, Codex, and unknown adapter behavior.\\nVerification: npm test -- tests/agent-invocation-lifecycle.test.ts (pass), npm test (pass). kspec validate currently reports pre-existing repo-level validation failures unrelated to this task.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJSA2TZWD88MG76PZ7KFKVFY\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Handle ACP permission requests in invocation — auto-approve tool calls in dispatch mode\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Root cause of agent hanging on Edit/Write/Bash calls: invocation.ts only registers a client.on('update') handler but never registers a client.on('request') handler. When claude-agent-acp sends a request_permission (or similar JSON-RPC request) asking the client to approve a tool call, the kspec ACP client has no handler — the request sits unanswered, the agent waits forever, and after 5 minutes the session/prompt times out.\\n\\nThe --dangerously-skip-permissions flag is irrelevant here — that is a Claude Code CLI flag. This adapter (claude-agent-acp) uses the Claude Agent SDK which has its own ACP-level permission protocol.\\n\\nFix: In src/agent-runtime/invocation.ts, register a 'request' handler on the ACP client alongside the existing 'update' handler. Auto-approve all permission requests in dispatch mode (auto_approve=true). In non-auto-approve mode, either deny or surface the request to the caller via onUpdate.\\n\\nThe ACPClient already has respondPermission(), respondReadTextFile(), respondWriteFile() methods — they just need to be wired up.\\n\\nRelevant files:\\n- src/agent-runtime/invocation.ts — add client.on('request', handler) around line 309\\n- src/acp/client.ts — respondPermission(), respond(), request event emission (line 99-100)\\n- src/acp/types.ts — RequestPermissionRequest, RequestPermissionResponse types\\n\\nVerify fix: kspec agent run worker --task @some-eligible-task should now complete Edit operations without hanging.\\n\\nSpec AC: @agent-invocation-lifecycle ac-11\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@agent-invocation-lifecycle\",\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #643. Registered ACP request handler in invocation.ts to auto-approve session/request_permission in dispatch mode. Fixes agent hang on Edit/Write/Bash tool calls.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"bug\",\n      \"agent\",\n      \"dispatch\",\n      \"acp\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"session_id\": \"01KJS9H76EZZB742ZEV9GGR8XB\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-03-03T07:37:29.340Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-03-03T07:40:03.365Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-03-03T07:49:11.078Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-03-03T17:11:49.924Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJSAQWYRAH4HBRZKMMAYHA0E\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-03T07:48:59.480Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented ACP permission request handler in invocation.ts.\\n\\nRoot cause: invocation.ts only registered a 'update' event handler but never registered a 'request' event handler. When the ACP agent sends a session/request_permission JSON-RPC request, it sat unanswered causing the agent to hang.\\n\\nFix: Added a 'request' handler that:\\n- In auto-approve mode: finds an allow_always or allow_once option and calls respondPermission with the selected optionId\\n- In non-auto-approve mode: denies with outcome cancelled\\n\\nAlso updated tests/mocks/acp-mock.js to support bidirectional RPC (agent→client requests), enabling integration tests via MOCK_ACP_SEND_PERMISSION_REQUEST=true.\\n\\nTests: 2 new tests in ac-11 section, all 32 tests pass. Shard 1 clean; shard 2 failure in enhanced-setup.test.ts is pre-existing on main (unrelated).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJSATPZHFFX6MMK7YKSYN008\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Fix pre-existing test failure: enhanced-setup codex config.toml not created\",\n    \"type\": \"bug\",\n    \"description\": \"Test: tests/enhanced-setup.test.ts > kspec setup (enhanced) > skill rendering > should render core skills to codex output when codex is detected\\n\\nError: ENOENT: no such file or directory, open '/tmp/.../.codex/config.toml'\\n\\nThe test expects kspec setup to create a .codex/config.toml file when codex is detected, but the file is not being created. The test reads codexConfigPath = path.join(tempDir, '.codex', 'config.toml') and checks it contains 'project_doc_fallback_filenames' and 'kspec-agents.md'.\\n\\nThis is a pre-existing failure on main (confirmed against main before PR #643 changes). Root cause: the setup command codex config writing logic is either not triggering, writing to a different path, or the detection logic is not working in the test environment.\\n\\nInvestigate: src/cli/setup.ts (or similar) to find where .codex/config.toml is written and why it is not being created in the temp dir fixture.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Already implemented on main in commit 5818b6315; verified by passing enhanced setup tests on 2026-03-04.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"bug\",\n      \"setup\",\n      \"codex\",\n      \"testing\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"session_id\": \"01KJWCX0B1M519AJ0RJVRJRT9C\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-03-03T07:50:31.664Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-03-04T12:26:19.906Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-03-04T12:26:21.507Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-03-04T12:26:22.555Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJSATY4AV9YYAYF2KEC7TF5F\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-03T07:50:38.986Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Pre-existing failure confirmed on main branch before any changes from task @01KJSA2T (PR #643). Verified by running: git stash && npx vitest run tests/enhanced-setup.test.ts and confirming the same ENOENT failure on the pristine main branch.\\n\\nFailure details:\\n- Test file: tests/enhanced-setup.test.ts:385\\n- Expects: .codex/config.toml to exist in temp dir\\n- Actual: file not created\\n- Error: ENOENT: no such file or directory\\n\\nThe setup command should write .codex/config.toml when codex is detected in the environment. The test simulates codex being present but the config file is never created.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJWD01DF0V2TMRBR8DXRXBQZ\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-04T12:26:06.639Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Verification on 2026-03-04:\\n- Confirmed fix already exists on main in commit 5818b6315 (fix: seed codex fallback docs with kspec-agents), which updates setup seeding and adds src/lib/codex-config.ts.\\n- Ran targeted reproduction: npx vitest run tests/enhanced-setup.test.ts -t 'should render core skills to codex output when codex is detected' (PASS).\\n- Ran full file: npx vitest run tests/enhanced-setup.test.ts (27 passed).\\nConclusion: task issue is already resolved upstream; no additional code changes required.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJTDBHV914S6MDRW4CDZ0YFP\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Implement kspec agent dispatch watch command\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@cli-agent-commands\",\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #645 (commit ec9d5b8). Implemented strict --retries validation for dispatch watch, fixed WebSocket global cleanup leakage in tests, and stabilized CLI regression tests. AC coverage for @cli-agent-commands ac-13..16 verified with green full test suite.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"cli\",\n      \"agent\",\n      \"dx\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"session_id\": \"01KJQT6EXAE3K8FTB2GW2ECCYF\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-03-03T17:53:55.048Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-03-03T20:13:47.469Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-03-03T20:13:48.571Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-03-03T20:13:49.590Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJTDBVQAZ0K2FGJ83BN3S107\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-03T17:54:05.163Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Two implementation pieces:\\n1. Daemon: in packages/daemon/src/routes/agent-dispatch.ts, pass onUpdate to runInvocation in the dispatch engine that broadcasts agent_text_chunk events via existing WebSocket PubSub (see createDispatchEngine - it already has pubsub.broadcast for InvocationEvents). Extend to broadcast { type: 'agent_text_chunk', session_id, agent_id, task_id, text, timestamp } on the 'agents' channel.\\n2. CLI: new kspec agent dispatch watch subcommand in src/cli/commands/agent.ts that connects to ws://localhost:<port>/ws, subscribes to the agents channel, filters and prints text chunks with [agent-id session-id] prefix, supports --agent and --session flags, auto-reconnects on drop with configurable retries.\\n\\nCovers: @cli-agent-commands ac-13, ac-14, ac-15, ac-16 and @daemon-agent-dispatch ac-8\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJTH90MA5MVVFYHBEDFZ981E\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-03T19:02:26.187Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented kspec agent dispatch watch command:\\n\\n1. Daemon side (packages/daemon/src/routes/agent-dispatch.ts): Added onTextChunk callback to createEngine, wiring pubsub.broadcast of agent_text_chunk events when dispatch engine produces text output.\\n\\n2. Core dispatch (src/agent-runtime/dispatch.ts): Added onTextChunk option to DispatchEngineOptions and DispatchEngine class. In _dispatchInvocation, passes onUpdate to runInvocation that calls onTextChunk for agent_message_chunk text updates.\\n\\n3. CLI (src/cli/commands/agent.ts): Added kspec agent dispatch watch subcommand with --agent, --session, --retries flags. Uses Node.js built-in WebSocket, subscribes to agents channel, filters agent_text_chunk events, prints with [agent-id session-id] prefix, auto-reconnects with exponential backoff, exits code 3 on failure/retry exhaustion.\\n\\n4. Tests: Added 6 new tests covering AC-13 (chunk prefix), AC-14 (reconnect + retry exhaustion), AC-15 (daemon not running), AC-16 (filter by agent/session). Used polling helper for timing-sensitive WebSocket mock tests.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJTJNVZHY3WW640N9P0ZWB6S\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-03T19:26:55.986Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Review findings: MUST-FIX: validate --retries input in agent dispatch watch; regression gate not green (full npm test has failing suites/timeouts).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJTHA450TCVJ7D7GMDQFGRCY\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Fix AC-10 test flakiness in cli-agent-commands\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Tests for AC-10 fail intermittently when a daemon from another parallel shard is running on port 3456. Error: 400 - undefined is not an object. Tests use kspec CLI subprocess which connects to any real daemon. Fix by mocking the daemon at CLI level or ensuring isolation.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@cli-agent-commands\",\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #672. Isolated AC-10 daemon dispatch tests by adding per-fixture daemon.auto_start=false config and forcing HOME/USERPROFILE to the temp project dir for subprocess CLI calls, eliminating external daemon leakage. Verified AC coverage for @cli-agent-commands ac-10 and @trait-error-guidance ac-1/ac-2 in tests/cli-agent-commands.test.ts; local full regression npm test passed and CI checks passed on current HEAD.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"cli\",\n      \"testing\",\n      \"bug\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"session_id\": \"01KJWD6PVCFRET92JHW9GRPE70\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-03-03T19:03:02.559Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-03-04T12:32:34.844Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-03-04T12:34:19.653Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-03-04T12:43:33.497Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJTPG6P49VG4TENB5ZGJ7JX4\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-03T20:33:44.644Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Automation status set to needs_review: Missing spec_ref; add/attach spec with AC coverage before automation\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJWDC0Q2SJG2AYE10SQYGVBE\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-04T12:32:39.138Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Execution context:\\n- Background: AC-10 tests for agent dispatch start can intermittently hit real daemon state in parallel runs.\\n- Scope: Stabilize AC-10 coverage in tests by removing external daemon dependencies.\\n- Files: tests/cli-agent-commands.test.ts (and minimal helper/support files only if required).\\n- Verification: run AC-10 focused test selection plus kspec validate.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJWDEDP1W65X8237823RSZS4\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-04T12:33:57.953Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented AC-10 test isolation in tests/cli-agent-commands.test.ts by creating a dedicated fixture setup that disables daemon auto_start via kspec.config.yaml and forces HOME/USERPROFILE to the temp project directory for subprocess runs. This removes leakage from external daemons running on 3456 in parallel shards.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJWDEJ8442MF9V882MEE3DMX\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-03-04T12:34:02.629Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Verification results: npx vitest run tests/cli-agent-commands.test.ts -t 'AC-10' passed repeatedly (10x loop), and full tests/cli-agent-commands.test.ts passed. kspec validate currently fails due unrelated pre-existing repo issues (duplicate @observations refs, missing .kspec/skills/observations/SKILL.md, existing alignment/completeness warnings).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJWDGRN647ACW1SX06RYNKQS\",\n        \"created_at\": \"